            "settings": {
                "label": "ABOUT THE MATERIAL",
                "heading": "<p>\"Wood-born down\"<br><em>has arrived.</em></p>",
                "body": "<p>Kapok is a seed fiber harvested from the pods of the kapok tree, native to Southeast Asia. KAPOK KNOT's breakthrough was transforming this centuries-old natural material into a high-performance insulation sheet — a first in the fashion industry.</p><p>The result: a fiber that is <strong>1/8th the weight of cotton</strong>, breathes naturally, generates warmth as it absorbs moisture, and leaves no animal or environmental harm in its wake.</p>"
